{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZ3BawbXjRNHp77xdtyuQz","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec11_data.tex has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17474a62-7527-453d-99c4-703178c27619","uuid":"6940fe13-f0e2-4ecd-9c6e-36427329e4e5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:16:58.739Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec11_data.tex","oldString":"\\paragraph{What this does not claim.} The statement above says what is\navailable and how it is checked, not that every reader will see the\nsame seconds: the timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the\nreplay's 33 minutes are one machine's, and only the counts, the hashes\nand the axiom lines are expected to repeat exactly.","newString":"\\paragraph{What this does not claim.} The statement above says what is\navailable and how it is checked. It does not say that every reader will see the\nsame seconds. The timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the\nreplay's 33 minutes are one machine's. Only the counts, the hashes\nand the axiom lines are expected to repeat exactly.","originalFile":"% The data, code and proofs statement, in paper 1's form (item 11, 2026-11-05).\n% Every path is in the repository; every number here is a section's and is\n% regenerated by the script that section names (paper3/README.md, \"How to\n% regenerate every number\").\n\\section*{Data, code and proofs}\n\\label{sec:data}\n\\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Data, code and proofs}\n\nOur scripts, logs, Lean files and the text of this paper are openly\navailable at \\url{https://github.com/Alex-Linhares/MOSP_trough_SAT},\nunder \\repofile{paper3/}, with the companion Lean under\n\\repofile{lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/}; the code and the\nproofs are open source under the MIT licence. Everything this paper\nreports can be re-run from there, and most of it can be checked without\nre-running. The repository holds:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item a script for every number in the paper, under\n  \\repofile{paper3/scripts/}, one per section\n  (Sections~\\ref{sec:statement}--\\ref{sec:related}); each reads the\n  manuscript's extract and the clone with plain file reads, executes\n  nothing of theirs, and has a \\texttt{-{}-check} mode that verifies every\n  page, line and quoted fragment the section cites and exits non-zero\n  if any has moved; \\repofile{paper3/README.md} lists the command beside\n  each number;\n\\item the replay of Section~\\ref{sec:replay}: the two sandbox scripts\n  and the two second-checker scripts verbatim, the launch commands and\n  the timeline (\\repofile{paper3/replay/README.md}), the short logs,\n  the axiom output, the version lines and the hashes\n  (\\repofile{paper3/replay/logs/}); the full build log and the exported\n  environment are too large to commit and are identified by their\n  SHA-256 hashes, which are committed, and a script\n  (\\repofile{paper3/replay/counts.sh}) that recomputes every count of\n  that section from the log;\n\\item the companion Lean of Section~\\ref{sec:lean}: the two files, the\n  axiom audit that prints the axioms of every declaration the paper\n  names (\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean}) with its committed\n  output, and the byte-level re-diff of the copied model against the\n  clone (\\repofile{paper3/lean/rediff.log}); Appendix~\\ref{app:lean}\n  lists the names;\n\\item the measurement of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}: every call's\n  seconds and result (\\repofile{paper3/latex/tables/practitioner_raw.csv}),\n  the versions, machine and load of the run of record\n  (\\repofile{paper3/latex/tables/practitioner_meta.json}), and the\n  script that regenerates the formulas from their seeds and re-runs it;\n\\item the two audits the paper rests on, with their scripts and the\n  committed text extract of the manuscript\n  (\\repofile{reports/scratch/eth_audit/}), and the four public texts\n  Section~\\ref{sec:related} quotes, as fetched, with their hashes\n  (\\repofile{paper3/related/fetched/});\n\\item the record of every question the writing could not settle, one\n  numbered entry each, in \\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD}; and the\n  report of the blind reading of the whole paper against its sources,\n  in \\repofile{paper3/refuter/}.\n\\end{itemize}\nThe object of the paper is not ours. The OpenAI collection is read-only\nat commit \\texttt{4eaee875} of \\url{https://github.com/openai/math}\n(Apache-2.0 licence); the challenge file, the solution tree, the scope\nnote and the manuscript are cited from it by file and line, and nothing\nin it was modified. A reader who wants to repeat the replay needs the\ncollection at that commit, the pinned Lean release and the Mathlib\nrevision Section~\\ref{sec:replay} names, a sandbox such as the one the\nscripts use, and about an hour of eight cores.\n\n\\paragraph{What this does not claim.} The statement above says what is\navailable and how it is checked, not that every reader will see the\nsame seconds: the timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the\nreplay's 33 minutes are one machine's, and only the counts, the hashes\nand the axiom lines are expected to repeat exactly.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":62,"oldLines":7,"newStart":62,"newLines":7,"lines":[" scripts use, and about an hour of eight cores."," "," \\paragraph{What this does not claim.} The statement above says what is","-available and how it is checked, not that every reader will see the","-same seconds: the timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the","-replay's 33 minutes are one machine's, and only the counts, the hashes","+available and how it is checked. It does not say that every reader will see the","+same seconds. The timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the","+replay's 33 minutes are one machine's. Only the counts, the hashes"," and the axiom lines are expected to repeat exactly."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NZ3BawbXjRNHp77xdtyuQz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
