{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WB8xAXDdyNYFe4dWS8e3tD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec12_ack.tex has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17474a62-7527-453d-99c4-703178c27619","uuid":"28453f86-64d9-4e7e-a4aa-624ea636a15b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:17:04.769Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec12_ack.tex","oldString":"AI's word for any result. The verified statement is what the Lean kernel\nand, in our replay, a second checker written independently of Lean\naccept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}); every number in the paper is printed\nby a script that a reader can run (the data statement above); every\nquotation carries the page and line, or the file and line, where it can\nbe read; and the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the\nextract, the audits and the logs, by a second session of the same\nassistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources, whose findings and\nwhat was done about each are on record\n(\\repofile{paper3/refuter/README.md}). ``People who checked'', in","newString":"AI's word for any result. The verified statement is what the Lean kernel\nand, in our replay, a second checker written independently of Lean\naccept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}). Every number in the paper is printed\nby a script that a reader can run (the data statement above). Every\nquotation carries the page and line, or the file and line, where it can\nbe read. And the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the\nextract, the audits and the logs, by a second session of the same\nassistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources. Its findings and\nwhat was done about each are on record\n(\\repofile{paper3/refuter/README.md}). ``People who checked'', in","originalFile":"% Acknowledgements, with the disclosure of AI use in paper 1's form\n% (paper1/latex/sec8_ack.tex), written by item 11 on 2026-11-05. The\n% software versions are those the sections record (Section 5 the replay,\n% Section 7 the measurement, Section 8 our library).\n\\section*{Acknowledgements}\n\\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Acknowledgements}\n\n\\paragraph{Use of AI tools.} Much of this work was carried out with Claude\nCode (Anthropic), an AI coding assistant running Claude models. Under the\nauthor's direction it wrote the scripts, the companion Lean files and the\ndrafts of the text, ran the sandboxed replay and the measurement, read\nthe manuscript and the Lean sources, and searched the few texts\nSection~\\ref{sec:related} names. The author chose the question, fixed\nthe title and the stance, directed the work, read the results and takes\nfull responsibility for the content of this paper. We did not take the\nAI's word for any result. The verified statement is what the Lean kernel\nand, in our replay, a second checker written independently of Lean\naccept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}); every number in the paper is printed\nby a script that a reader can run (the data statement above); every\nquotation carries the page and line, or the file and line, where it can\nbe read; and the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the\nextract, the audits and the logs, by a second session of the same\nassistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources, whose findings and\nwhat was done about each are on record\n(\\repofile{paper3/refuter/README.md}). ``People who checked'', in\nSection~\\ref{sec:intro}, means the author and that assistant.\n\n\\paragraph{The object of the paper.} The theorem, the proof and the\nmanuscript this paper reads are OpenAI's\n\\citep{OAI:The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026},\npublished under the Apache-2.0 licence in a collection whose checking\ntool \\citep{LeanComparator} and scope notes made the exact reading\npossible. Nothing in this paper is a claim of a flaw in that work.\n\n\\paragraph{Software.} The replay used the Lean release the collection\npins, Lean~4.34.1 \\citep{MouraUllrich2021}, with the Mathlib library\n\\citep{Mathlib2020} at the revision the collection pins, inside the\n\\texttt{bwrap} sandbox Section~\\ref{sec:replay} describes; the second\nchecker was \\texttt{nanoda\\_lib} \\citep{Nanoda} on an export written by\n\\texttt{lean4export} \\citep{Lean4Export}. Our own library builds with\nLean~4.34.0-rc2 and Mathlib (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}). The measurement\nused CaDiCaL~1.9.5 \\citep{Biere2024CaDiCaL} through PySAT\n\\citep{Ignatiev2018PySAT}, Ganak~2.8.0 \\citep{Sharma2019Ganak} and\nApproxMC~4.4.0 \\citep{Chakraborty2013ApproxMC, Soos2019BIRD}. The\nbibliography's DOIs were checked against Crossref and DataCite\n(\\repofile{paper3/latex/doi_check.log}).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":12,"newStart":15,"newLines":12,"lines":[" full responsibility for the content of this paper. We did not take the"," AI's word for any result. The verified statement is what the Lean kernel"," and, in our replay, a second checker written independently of Lean","-accept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}); every number in the paper is printed","-by a script that a reader can run (the data statement above); every","+accept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}). Every number in the paper is printed","+by a script that a reader can run (the data statement above). Every"," quotation carries the page and line, or the file and line, where it can","-be read; and the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the","+be read. And the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the"," extract, the audits and the logs, by a second session of the same","-assistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources, whose findings and","+assistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources. Its findings and"," what was done about each are on record"," (\\repofile{paper3/refuter/README.md}). ``People who checked'', in"," Section~\\ref{sec:intro}, means the author and that assistant."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WB8xAXDdyNYFe4dWS8e3tD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
