er's decision recorded in\n\\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD}, S3); the axiom audit is\n\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean} with its committed log\n\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.log}, and the byte-level re-diff of the\ncopy against the comparator file is \\repofile{paper3/scripts/lean_rediff.py}\nwith its log \\repofile{paper3/lean/rediff.log}. Every row's declarations are\non the three standard axioms \\texttt{propext}, \\texttt{Classical.choice},\n\\texttt{Quot.sound} or fewer; none depends on \\texttt{sorryAx}. Nothing from\nthe other study that shares the directory is cited.\n\n\\begin{longtable}{@{}p{0.07\\linewidth}p{0.43\\linewidth}p{0.44\\linewidth}@{}}\n\\toprule\n & result & Lean names \\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endhead\n\\leangroup{The copy (\\texttt{PrimitiveMachine.lean}, lines 31--221 = comparator lines 1--190 and 220, byte-identical; definitions only, the namespaces of the source kept)}\n\\leanentry{copy-model}{The comparator's vocabulary: formulas and their satisfying-assignment count, the canonical bit encoding and its length, the multitape machine with its step and start, the trace, the running-time scale \\(\\rhon\\) and the bound built from it, the count word, the located step and the visited space} \\leannames{OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT.count, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.encodeCNF, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding.formulaBitLength, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.PrimitiveMachine.step, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation.Trace, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.countWord, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.locatedStep, OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.visitedSpace} \\\\\n\\leangroup{The restatement (\\texttt{Frame.lean}): two \\texttt{def}s of a \\texttt{Prop}, never proved, never axioms}\n\\leanentry{subexpcount}{The comparator statement for width \\(k\\) as a named \\texttt{Prop}, \\(\\SubexpCount\\ k\\): its body is the comparator theorem's body, identical after whitespace normalisation (1,073 characters, 23 lines)} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.SubexpCount} \\\\\n\\leanentry{exactcountandsat}{The comparator theorem in full: for every \\(k \\ge 2\\), \\(\\SubexpCount\\ k\\)} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.ExactCountAndSat} \\\\\n\\leangroup{What is proved about them (\\texttt{Frame.lean})}\n\\leanentry{subexpcount-anti}{A machine for width \\(k\\) is a machine for every width \\(k' \\le k\\), with the same constants; and the unpacking of the ``for every \\(k \\ge 2\\)'' form} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.SubexpCount.anti, MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount} \\\\\n\\leanentry{runtimebound-eq}{The bound unfolds, by definition, to \\(C\\,(L+1)^d\\,2^{A\\cdot\\rhon}\\)} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.runtimeBound_eq} \\\\\n\\leanentry{rho-little-o}{\\(\\rhon = o(n)\\): the verified exponent is subexponential in the limit, from \\((\\ln y)^2/\\sqrt{y} \\to 0\\)} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt, MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.runtimeScale_isLittleO} \\\\\n\\leanentry{is-subexp-exponent}{``\\(f\\) is a subexponential exponent'' means \\(f = o(n)\\); \\(A \\cdot \\rhon\\) is one for every constant \\(A\\)} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.IsSubexpExponent, MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale} \\\\\n\\leanentry{trace-projection}{A run of the located (cell-monitoring) step projects to a run of the plain step with the same number of steps, so the comparator's time bound is a bound on the machine itself} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.LocatedCfg.monitor_config, MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.Trace.config_of_locatedStep} \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{longtable}\n\\endgroup\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":11,"newStart":5,"newLines":11,"lines":[" \\begingroup\\sloppy"," "," Every Lean name the paper cites, with its file under","-\\repofile{lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/} (the files are left where","+\\repofile{lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/}. The files are left where"," loop0014 wrote them, by the owner's decision recorded in","-\\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD}, S3); the axiom audit is","+\\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD}, S3. The axiom audit is"," \\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean} with its committed log","-\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.log}, and the byte-level re-diff of the","+\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.log}. The byte-level re-diff of the"," copy against the comparator file is \\repofile{paper3/scripts/lean_rediff.py}"," with its log \\repofile{paper3/lean/rediff.log}. Every row's declarations are"," on the three standard axioms \\texttt{propext}, \\texttt{Classical.choice},"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019em3siuxj9Xc7EcrAcNAnx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
