of the thirty-nine are bibliographic or typographic: S2, 02b,\n02d, 05c, 06c, 08a, 08b, 08c, 11g, and the five spelling, placement and\ntagging choices of 02a, 03a, 03d, 04a, 08xa. The rest are choices\nabout what the text says. Each is a sentence that can be struck\nwithout touching any number.\n\n'''\nt=t[:start]+new+t[end:]\nold_nc='''\\\\item \\\\textbf{The list of open questions is complete to the day it was\n  written.} Entries added after it, by the reading of the whole paper\n  that follows this draft, are in the file and not here.'''\nassert old_nc in t\nt=t.replace(old_nc,'''\\\\item \\\\textbf{The list of open questions is complete to the day it was\n  last re-counted}, 2026-11-05, and includes the entries of the reading\n  of the whole paper and of the final pass. Any entry added after that\n  day is in the file and not here.''')\nopen(f,'w').write(t)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngrep -n \"sixty-one\\|thirty-nine\\|Twenty-two\\|Fifteen are\" sec10_conclusion.tex | head","description":"Rewrite the conclusion's open-questions subsection with all 61 entries re-sorted"}}}
