pository's README, and since here too; 11e, a paragraph for the","+repository's instructions file, drafted and not applied; 11f, the","+plan's record of what was done; 12a and 12b, the scope of the final","+pass and this list's own re-count. The thirty-nine below affect the","+text and are open. In each case the text stands as chosen, and the","+entry says what would change."," "," \\begin{description}\\setlength{\\itemsep}{1pt}"," \\item[The title and its figures.] S2: $2^n$ is typeset with a"]},{"oldStart":82,"oldLines":7,"newStart":90,"newLines":10,"lines":["   PDF's metadata. 02a: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} carries both the","   two-panel Figure~\\ref{fig:central} and Figure~\\ref{fig:runtime-scale},","   three drawings of one function. 02b: the central figure's peak is","-  placed analytically and its legend carries the $+16$.","+  placed analytically and its legend carries the $+16$. 10b: the","+  title's ``is slower'' is reconciled with the paper's non-claim of any","+  running time by Sections~\\ref{sec:statement} and","+  \\ref{sec:practitioner}, and by nothing in the title itself."," \\item[The statement (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}).] 02c: a proof-side","   fact, the constant $256 + A_t$, is quoted in the statement section","   for its value. 02d: the Lean theorem is transcribed as a display, not"]},{"oldStart":115,"oldLines":9,"newStart":126,"newLines":9,"lines":[" \\item[For the practitioner (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}).] 06a: the","   two guarantee curves share one scale factor, so that they cross where","   the statement puts the crossing. 06c: seven references for the tools","-  and the threshold are from memory, with no DOI checked. 06d: the","-  counters are reported at their defaults, including a plateau that","-  looks like a preprocessing budget.","+  and the threshold were typed from memory; their DOIs have since been","+  checked (10a). 06d: the counters are reported at their defaults,","+  including a plateau that looks like a preproc