(\\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/NativeLargeEntry.lean},\n   250\tlines 11--33) supplies a trace of length at most\n   251\t\\texttt{runtimeBound C A d L n} (line~27) with $1 \\le C \\wedge 1 \\le A$\n   252\t(line~12). Its exponent constant is \\texttt{256 + At} (line~51), where\n   253\t\\texttt{At} comes from the leaf program's uniform contract\n   254\t(\\path{NativeLeafContract.uniform_contract}, line~39; the contract\n   255\tgives $1 \\le \\mathtt{At}$, \\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/NativeLeafContract.lean},\n   256\tline~793), and its cutoff is \\texttt{max 20 (max Nleaf Ns)} (line~50),\n   257\twith \\texttt{Ns} obtained non-constructively from an eventual inequality\n   258\t(\\path{Filter.eventually_atTop}, line~48). The $2^{A\\cdot\\mathtt{runtimeScale}\\,n}$\n   259\tfactor is assembled by \\path{runtime_of_tree_and_leaf} (line~46)\n   260\tfrom the DFS visit bound of \\path{Native.outer_from_setup}\n   261\t(\\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/NativeOuter.lean}, lines 53--56: visits at most\n   262\ta square polynomial in $n$ times $2^{n/\\mathtt{sparsifySchedule}\\,n}$)\n   263\tand the leaf time. For $n \\le \\mathtt{cutoff}$,\n   264\t\\path{Native.entry_small_primitive}\n   265\t(\\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/NativeEntry.lean}, lines 81--100) gives\n   266\t$\\mathtt{time} \\le 28700\\,(L+1)^2$ (line~92) through the finite scanner\n   267\tof \\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/FiniteFallback.lean}. The two branches are\n   268\tfolded by \\texttt{runtime\\_with\\_fallback} and\n   269\t\\texttt{space\\_with\\_fallback}\n   270\t(\\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/NativeOuterBudgets.lean}, lines 297 and 317)\n   271\tinto one triple, and the witnesses the final theorem exhibits are\n   272\t\\texttt{C + 28700, A + 1, S + 5022741, d + 2, e + 2}\n   273\t(\\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean}, line~41). So the proof as written\n   274\thas an exponent constant of at least $258$ in front of $\\rhon$, a\n   275\tpolynomial degree \\texttt{d} that depends on $k$ (line~51: $\\mathtt{db} + (4(k-2)+2) + \