cks ABI.countStack = countWord (SAT.count F)} and\n   305\t\\texttt{final.stacks ABI.answerStack = [decide (0 < SAT.count F)]} from\n   306\tthe canonical DFS execution, and\n   307\t\\path{Native.counting_primitive_from_entry} (line~73) transports\n   308\tboth to the primitive machine's tapes; \\texttt{countWord\\_toNat} and\n   309\t\\texttt{countWord\\_count\\_length} supply the decoding and length clauses\n   310\tof the statement.\n   311\t\n   312\t\\paragraph{The statement match, counted.} The solution file does not\n   313\timport the challenge file: \\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean} begins\n   314\t(lines 1--3) with \\texttt{NativeLargeEntry}, \\texttt{SqrtLogSpace.Statement}\n   315\tand \\texttt{SqrtLog.StatementCanonical}. The library re-declares every\n   316\tdefinition the statement uses under the same fully qualified names, in\n   317\tseven files: the SAT vocabulary in \\clonefile{SAT.lean}, the bit\n   318\tarithmetic in \\clonefile{BinaryArithmetic.lean}, the nine encoding\n   319\tfunctions in \\clonefile{Encoding.lean}, the machine in\n   320\t\\clonefile{Computation.lean}, \\texttt{runtimeScale} and\n   321\t\\texttt{runtimeBound} in \\clonefile{SqrtLog/StatementScale.lean}, the\n   322\tspace instrumentation in \\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/VisitedTape.lean} and\n   323\t\\texttt{countWord} in \\clonefile{SqrtLogSpace/EncodingBounds.lean}\n   324\t(line~17, the challenge's line~147). The definition diff compares 35\n   325\tdeclarations: 33 are identical character for character after whitespace\n   326\tnormalisation, and the remaining two, \\texttt{runtimeScale} and\n   327\t\\texttt{runtimeBound}, differ only in that the challenge writes\n   328\t\\texttt{noncomputable def} where the library opens a\n   329\t\\texttt{noncomputable section} (\\clonefile{SqrtLog/StatementScale.lean},\n   330\tline~15). The theorem statement itself, from \\texttt{theorem","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta