e exception is the   replay (item 01), which builds a **fresh copy** of the clone,   `~/dev/untrusted/replay/openai-math/`, inside a `bwrap` sandbox;   nothing produced inside the sandbox is executed outside it, and only   text (logs, `#print axioms` output, hashes) is copied out. - **The sandbox, as it is running.** The coordinator started the replay   on 2026-11-05 at 01:03: `~/dev/untrusted/replay/run_sandbox.sh` runs   `bwrap` under `nice -n 19` with `/usr /lib /lib64 /bin /sbin /etc`   read-only, a `tmpfs` `/home` with `/home/al` bound to `replay/home`   (the repository `/home/al/dev/MOSP` is invisible), `replay/` at   `/replay`, `--unshare-pid --unshare-ipc --unshare-uts   --die-with-parent`, network on for the lakefile's clone hooks and the   `elan`/Mathlib downloads; inside it `replay.sh` installs `elan` into   the private home (`ELAN_HOME=/home/al/.elan` inside = `replay/home/.elan`   outside; the pinned `v4.34.1` fetched), runs `lake exe cache get`, then   `lake build OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Main -j 8` (the   3,091-module closure only), then `#print axioms` of   `exact_count_and_sat` through `lake env lean`, and writes the exit code   to `replay/logs/DONE`. Logs: `replay/logs/sandbox.out`,   `build_main.log` (large, git-ignored; its SHA-256 and filtered tail are   committed), `build_filtered.log`, `axioms.log`. **Item 01 does not   start another build**: it waits for `DONE` with bounded foreground   polls, reads the logs, and relaunches `run_sandbox.sh` once only on a   failure it has diagnosed and fixed inside `replay/`. Anything else that   *runs* OpenAI's code — `lean4export`, nanoda on the export — runs   through the same `bwrap` line, by a second script beside `replay.sh`,   and its invocation is recorded in `paper3/replay/README.md` before it   runs. - **Subagents: at most 4 per session, total.** One refuter at a time, for   a second reading of a section or a statement; never fan-out per target. - **A measurement is not a theorem.** Item 06'