lSAT closure is 3,091 modules /   550,551 lines: **the build is budgeted at up to 8 hours**, and the   section says so. - The replay (item 01) runs in the **foreground with bounded polls**   (`timeout` on each poll, never a background wait that ends the turn);   its item carries `[cap 8 h]` on its first line, which the driver reads   as that item's wall-clock cap (`loop.py`, `item_cap`); every other item   runs under `iteration_cap_hours` = 4. - Only one `lake build` of **our** `lean/` at a time (the loop is   sequential; never start a second in the background). The sandbox's   replay is a separate tree and may build concurrently: 32 cores and   121 GB are enough for both at `nice -n 19`, so the gate runs after   every session as usual, replay or no replay. - Nothing is downloaded beyond: the sandbox's `elan`, toolchain, Mathlib   cache and the lakefile's dependency clones (inside the sandbox only,   by the running `replay.sh`); nanoda and `lean4export` sources if item   01 or 12 attempts the second-kernel replay (built and run inside the   sandbox); `pip install` of a model counter for   item 06 if one is available; the arXiv abstract page of 2608.14673 and   the comparator and nanoda READMEs for item 08 (quoted only if fetched;   otherwise \"reported\").  ## Current Focus Item 01 is the replay and has the longest cap; the build itself was started by the coordinator before launch (see above), so item 01 waits, reads, records and attempts nanoda; it is first because every later section says \"replayed\" or \"not replayed\" depending on it. Items 02–04 are the exact reading (the statement, what the manuscript claims beyond it, the proof inspection joined with the replay). Items 05–06 are the consequences (which hypotheses fall, what a derived lower bound loses; the practitioner's comparison). Item 07 is the companion Lean (our restatement, audited). Item 08 is related work. Items 09–11 write the abstract, introduction, conclusion, the refuter pass, and the write-up around the paper. Item 12 is the reserve (nanoda if item 01 could not do it, or whichever item ended short).  ## Target Items (in order) See `iterations.md`. Dependency order: 01 → 02 → 03 → 04 → 05 → 06 → 07 → 08 → 09 → 10 → 11 → 12; items 02–08 depend on 01 only through the one sentence \"replayed / not replayed\", which item 04 writes from `paper3/replay/`.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - The item's section is drafted in `paper3/latex/sec*.tex`, builds under   `make -C paper3/latex check` (no undefined reference or citation), and   ends with \"what this does not claim\". - Every number in the section names its regenerate command; every quote   names page and line. - Every `ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD` entry the item wrote is dated and has the three   parts (ambiguity, choice, what the owner may change). - Lean (item 07 and any item that touches a theorem): `lake build` clean,   imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, the   axiom audit run (`paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean`, the   `paper1/axiom_check.lean` pattern) with every line on   `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`. - `python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0015/gate.py` passes. - PROGRESS.md has the iteration's section; `iterations.md` has the item   marked.  ## Completion Conditions - All twelve items marked (`[x]`, or `[!]` with the gap stated in the   text and in `ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`). - `paper3/latex/main.pdf` builds clean with the title verbatim, every   section present, the refuter pass (item 10) applied or recorded. - `paper3/README.md` complete (what the paper is, how to build, how to   regenerate every number, the replay's status, the CLAUDE.md paragraph   drafted in its last section and **not applied** to CLAUDE.md). - `reports/paper3_plan.md` §0 updated by item 11 with what was done.  ## Context - `reports/paper3_plan.md`: the plan this loop executes (§0.1 the question   and the stance, §0.3 what is on record, §0.4 the design decisions, §0.5   the items, §0.6 the budget rule, §0.7 the ris